# Pin line endings for files whose BYTES are load-bearing.
#
# `tauri-plugin-sql` embeds each migration with `include_str!` at build time
# and sqlx stores a SHA-384 of that text in `_sqlx_migrations`. At boot it
# re-hashes the embedded text and refuses to start if it differs:
#
#     migration 12 was previously applied but has been modified
#
# The hash is over raw bytes, so CRLF and LF are different migrations as far
# as sqlx is concerned - without this file, whether a build embeds CRLF or LF
# depends on the `core.autocrlf` setting of whichever machine checked the
# repo out. That is how `migration-v12.sql` came to sit in a Windows working
# tree as CRLF while the committed blob (and every database already in the
# field) was LF, leaving locally built binaries unable to open an existing
# database.
#
# Pinning to LF makes the embedded bytes identical on every developer machine
# and on all three CI runners, and matches what is already applied.
#
# NOTE: normalising an ALREADY-APPLIED migration would break databases in the
# field just as surely as editing one. These files are LF in git today, so
# this pins the status quo rather than changing it. Verify before adding a
# rule that would rewrite an existing migration.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Default handling for everything else: normalise text in the repo, leave the
# working tree to the platform.
* text=auto
